# Optional file references only; the browser and private helper own their lifetime.
# Invoke Function FvwmXFilesWithTransfers from your existing menu or binding.
# Every Paste/drop needs explicit confirmation before a Copy or Move job.
AddToFunc FvwmXFilesWithTransfers I Exec exec fvwm-file-browser --file-transfer

# List focus: Ctrl-C Copy, Ctrl-X Cut, Ctrl-V Paste. Drag to an XDND target;
# Shift requests Move. The receiving browser uses its displayed directory.
# Alt-Y confirms a received operation; Alt-Z cancels the confirmation.
# Copied references survive folder navigation, and end with this browser.
# Ordinary file paths are supported; no text/image clipboard history is implied.

# If using the optional FileManager1 service, add --file-transfer to its one
# existing service definition, for example:
# AddToFunc StartFunction I Exec exec fvwm-file-browser --filemanager-service --file-transfer
# A competing service is never replaced. D-Bus is optional for ordinary browsing.
